.TH AC 1 "2026" "ac 0.1.0" "A language"
.SH NAME
ac \- compiler for the A programming language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ac
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIsource.a\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ac
compiles A source code directly to a native executable. It is written entirely in
x86-64 assembly, needs no assembler, linker or C library, and can produce programs
for Linux (x86-64, ARM64, RISC-V 64, LoongArch64), Windows (x86-64) and Android (ARM64, x86-64, RISC-V 64).
.PP
A has C-like syntax: variables, constants, functions, structs, classes with
public/private members, enums, modules, pointers, arrays and the usual control flow.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " FILE"
Write the executable to FILE. By default the file is named
\fINAME\fR\-\fIVERSION\fR\-\fIRELEASE\fR.\fIEXT\fR, for example hello\-1\-debug.elf.
.TP
.BI \-t " TARGET"
Target platform: \fBlinux\fR (default, x86-64), \fBlinux\-arm64\fR, \fBwindows\fR (x86-64),
\fBandroid\fR (ARM64), \fBandroid\-x64\fR, \fBlinux\-riscv64\fR, \fBandroid\-riscv64\fR or \fBlinux\-loongarch64\fR.
.TP
.BI \-D " NAME[=VALUE]"
Define a preprocessor macro (the value is 1 when omitted). May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-E
Print the preprocessed source to standard output and stop.
.TP
.BI \-v " CODE"
Version code used in the default output name (default 1).
.TP
.BI \-r " TYPE"
Release type used in the default output name, for example debug or release (default debug).
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show a short help text.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the compiler version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I lib/ , /usr/lib/a/ , /usr/local/lib/a/
Directories searched for modules named in \fBimport\fR statements, after the
directory of the importing file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ac hello.a                      # hello-1-debug.elf
ac \-t windows \-r release hello.a  # hello-1-release.exe
ac \-t android \-o hello hello.a    # ARM64 binary for adb / Termux
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when the source has an error (a message with the source line is
printed on standard error).
.SH AUTHOR
Aytict, https://aytict.fi
